Wei Zhao, Mingyue Shang, Yang Liu, Liang Wang, and Jingming Liu. 2020.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Ape210k: A large-scale and template-rich dataset of math word problems.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib53.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2009.11506</em>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib54" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhou et al. (2025)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Yihe Zhou, Tao Ni, Wei-Bin Lee, and Qingchuan Zhao. 2025.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">A survey on backdoor threats in large language models (llms): Attacks, defenses, and evaluations.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib54.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">arXiv preprint arXiv:2502.05224</em>.

</span></li>
      
<li id="bib.bib55" class="ltx_bibitem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_role_refnum ltx_tag_bibitem">Zhu et al. (2022)</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">
Biru Zhu, Yujia Qin, Ganqu Cui, Yangyi Chen, Weilin Zhao, Chong Fu, Yangdong Deng, Zhiyuan Liu, Jingang Wang, Wei Wu, and 1 others. 2022.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock">Moderate-fitting as a natural backdoor defender for pre-trained language models.

</span>
<span class="ltx_bibblock"><em id="bib.bib55.1" class="ltx_emph ltx_font_italic">Advances in Neural Information Processing Systems</em>, 35:1086–1099.

</span></li>
    
</ul>
</section>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="A1" class="ltx_appendix">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_appendix"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_appendix">Appendix A </span>Proofs</h2>

<div id="A1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we provide detailed proofs for Definitions <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Overview of Poison-to-Poison ‣ 4 P2P Framework ‣ P2P: A Poison-to-Poison Remedy for Reliable Backdoor Defense in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a> and <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Overview of Poison-to-Poison ‣ 4 P2P Framework ‣ P2P: A Poison-to-Poison Remedy for Reliable Backdoor Defense in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>. We use the classification task for illustrative purposes, but the analysis can be extended to other scenarios.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p2.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p2.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Definition <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Overview of Poison-to-Poison ‣ 4 P2P Framework ‣ P2P: A Poison-to-Poison Remedy for Reliable Backdoor Defense in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>:</span>
Let the original label space be:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}=\{0,1,\dots,n-1\}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}=\{0,1,\dots,n-1\},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">and the extended label space can be represented as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}=\{0,1,\dots,2n-1\}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>,</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">…</mi><mo>,</mo><mrow><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi></mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}=\{0,1,\dots,2n-1\}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Let the original model be <math id="A1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g:X\to\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g:X\to\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, with accuracy defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex12" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}(g)=\Pr[g(X)=Y],\quad(X,Y)\sim\mathcal{D}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="1.167em">,</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}(g)=\Pr[g(X)=Y],\quad(X,Y)\sim\mathcal{D}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.4" class="ltx_p">Let the benign-trigger injection be <math id="A1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\phi(x)=\tau(\delta,x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>τ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>δ</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\phi(x)=\tau(\delta,x)</annotation></semantics></math>.
Introduce a label embedding <math id="A1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="e:Y\to Y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">e:Y\to Y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math> and a projection <math id="A1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi:Y^{\prime}\to Y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi>Y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi:Y^{\prime}\to Y</annotation></semantics></math>.
For the P2P model <math id="A1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f:X\to Y^{\prime}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><msup><mi>Y</mi><mo>′</mo></msup></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f:X\to Y^{\prime}</annotation></semantics></math>, define its P2P accuracy as follows:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex13" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(X)))=Y]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>P2P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(X)))=Y].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.5" class="ltx_p">Take any optimal original function:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g^{\star}\in\arg\max_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo>∈</mo><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><munder><mi>max</mi><mi>g</mi></munder><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g^{\star}\in\arg\max_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.6" class="ltx_p">and construct the corresponding P2P function:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\phi(x))=e(g^{\star}(x))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mi>e</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\phi(x))=e(g^{\star}(x)).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.7" class="ltx_p">Then for any <math id="A1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> we have:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex16" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi(f(\phi(x)))=g^{\star}(x)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi(f(\phi(x)))=g^{\star}(x),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.8" class="ltx_p">it follows that:</p>
<table id="A1.EGx2" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="A1.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>P2P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex17.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(X)))=Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(X)))=Y]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex18"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex18.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\Pr[g^{\star}(X)=Y]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mo>⋆</mo></msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\Pr[g^{\star}(X)=Y]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="A1.Ex19"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="A1.Ex19.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\sup_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>g</mi></munder><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\sup_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.9" class="ltx_p">On the other hand, for any <math id="A1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math>, define its corresponding projection function:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex20" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex20.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="g_{f}(x):=\pi(f(\phi(x)))." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mi>π</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">g_{f}(x):=\pi(f(\phi(x))).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.10" class="ltx_p">Then,</p>
<table id="A1.Ex21" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex21.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\Pr[g_{f}(X)=Y]\leq\sup_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>P2P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><msub><mi>g</mi><mi>f</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>X</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Y</mi><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">≤</mo><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>g</mi></munder><mi>Acc</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\Pr[g_{f}(X)=Y]\leq\sup_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p2.11" class="ltx_p">Thus, the P2P algorithm has the potential to achieve performance not inferior to that of the original algorithm:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex22" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex22.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\sup_{f}\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\sup_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">sup</mo><mi>f</mi></munder><mrow><msub><mi>Acc</mi><mi>P2P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.1389em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0.1389em" movablelimits="false" rspace="0.167em">sup</mo><mi>g</mi></munder><mrow><mi>Acc</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\sup_{f}\mathrm{Acc}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\sup_{g}\mathrm{Acc}(g).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="A1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="A1.p3.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="A1.p3.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proof of Definition <a href="#S4.SS1" title="4.1 Overview of Poison-to-Poison ‣ 4 P2P Framework ‣ P2P: A Poison-to-Poison Remedy for Reliable Backdoor Defense in LLMs" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.1</span></a>:</span>
In the data-poisoning backdoor attacks, the ASR is defined as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex23" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex23.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{ASR}(g)=\Pr[g(x)=y_{\text{target}}]," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>ASR</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>g</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ASR}(g)=\Pr[g(x)=y_{\text{target}}],</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the input containing an unknown trigger. The ASR of the P2P algorithm can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex24" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex24.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\mathrm{ASR}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(x)))=y_{\text{target}}]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>ASR</mi><mi>P2P</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ASR}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(x)))=y_{\text{target}}].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.3" class="ltx_p">Since the model <math id="A1.p3.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>f</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f</annotation></semantics></math> is optimized during training to map samples with the benign trigger <math id="A1.p3.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math> to the extended label <math id="A1.p3.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}\!\setminus\!\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}\!\setminus\!\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>, we have:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f(\phi(x))\in\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}\setminus\mathcal{Y}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>ϕ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>∈</mo><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo>∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f(\phi(x))\in\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}\setminus\mathcal{Y},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<table id="A1.Ex26" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(x)))=y_{\text{target}}]\approx 0." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>Pr</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mi>π</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>ϕ</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow><mo>≈</mo><mn>0</mn><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\Pr[\pi(f(\phi(x)))=y_{\text{target}}]\approx 0.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p3.4" class="ltx_p">In other words, the learning process of P2P diverts the effect of the attack trigger into the new label space, thereby weakening the effectiveness of the target label <math id="A1.p3.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<div id="A1.p4" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">In the testing phase, when the input contains the benign trigger <math id="A1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\delta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>δ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\delta</annotation></semantics></math>, the model output can be divided into two cases:</p>
<ul id="A1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="A1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Falls into the extended label space <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}\!\setminus\!\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>′</mo></msup><mo lspace="0.052em" rspace="0.052em">∖</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}^{\prime}\!\setminus\!\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>: its probability is denoted by <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and the probability that the model predicts <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.I1.i1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math>;</p>
</div></li>
<li id="A1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="A1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="A1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Falls into the original label space <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}</annotation></semantics></math>: its probability is <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="1-\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">1-\alpha</annotation></semantics></math>, and the probability that the model predicts <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{\text{target}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mtext>target</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{\text{target}}</annotation></semantics></math> is <math id="A1.I1.i2.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
<p id="A1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Therefore, the ASR of the P2P algorithm can be expressed as:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex27" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathrm{ASR}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\alpha\cdot\epsilon+(1-\alpha)\cdot\beta." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>ASR</mi><mi>P2P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>α</mi></mrow><mo rspace="0.055em" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi>β</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathrm{ASR}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f)=\alpha\cdot\epsilon+(1-\alpha)\cdot\beta.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.3" class="ltx_p">Ideally, <math id="A1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\alpha" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>α</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\alpha</annotation></semantics></math> approaches 1 while <math id="A1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\epsilon" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>ϵ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\epsilon</annotation></semantics></math> approaches 0 after sufficient training, and thus:</p>
<table id="A1.Ex28" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="A1.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lim_{t\to\infty}\mathrm{ASR}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f_{t})=0," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">lim</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>ASR</mi><mi>P2P</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lim_{t\to\infty}\mathrm{ASR}_{\mathrm{P2P}}(f_{t})=0,</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="A1.p4.4" class="ltx_p">where <math id="A1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{t}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{t}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the model after the <math id="A1.p4.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="t" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>t</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">t</annotation></semantics></math>-th iteration.</p>
</div>
<figure id="A1.T7" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 7: </span>Results of the P2P algorithm with different output verbalizer tokens. The token_1 denotes <span id="A1.T7.7" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">numeric tokens</span>, and token_2 uses <span id="A1.T7.8" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">negative</span>, <span id="A1.T7.9" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">positive</span>, <span id="A1.T7.10" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">bad</span>, and <span id="A1.T7.11" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">good</span> as verbalizer tokens.</figcaption>
<div id="A1.T7.12" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_center ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:310.5pt;height:57.7pt;vertical-align:-27.4pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-109.8pt,20.4pt) scale(0.585818924665569,0.585818924665569) ;">
<table id="A1.T7.12.1" class="ltx_tabular ltx_align_middle">
<tr id="A1.T7.12.1.1" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" rowspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Method</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">BadNets</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">AddSent</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">SynAttack</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.6.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">ProAttack</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.7.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">CbaAttack</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.1.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_tt" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" colspan="2"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.1.8.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MtbaAttack</span></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.12.1.2" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">CA<math id="A1.T7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">ASR<math id="A1.T7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">CA<math id="A1.T7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">ASR<math id="A1.T7.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">CA<math id="A1.T7.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.6" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">ASR<math id="A1.T7.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.7" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">CA<math id="A1.T7.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.8" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">ASR<math id="A1.T7.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.9" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">CA<math id="A1.T7.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.10" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">ASR<math id="A1.T7.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.11" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">CA<math id="A1.T7.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\uparrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#FF0000;" mathcolor="#FF0000" stretchy="false">↑</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\uparrow</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.2.12" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">ASR<math id="A1.T7.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\downarrow" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#0000FF;" mathcolor="#0000FF" stretchy="false">↓</mo><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\downarrow</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="A1.T7.12.1.3" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;" rowspan="3"><span id="A1.T7.12.1.3.1.1" class="ltx_text">Qwen-3</span></td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">Attack</td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.3.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">94.56</td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.3.4" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_r ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">99.78</td>
<td id="A1.T7.12.1.3.5" class="ltx_td ltx_align_center ltx_border_t" style="padding-left:5.1pt;padding-right:5.1pt;">93.96</td>
